From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:40:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Take the quartz transform locks in streaming order
 when cleaning up.

strmbase holds the filter's stream_cs around Receive() and EndOfStream(),
which then take receive_cs. transform_cleanup_stream() took receive_cs
first and then stream_cs, so stopping the graph while the streaming
thread was entering Receive() deadlocked both threads. This became
reachable for MPEG-1 audio in GE-Proton11-8, when the MPEG Audio Decoder
started being selected over the ACM wrapper; releasing an AMStream
multimedia stream (e.g. skipping a video) could then hang forever.

Take stream_cs before receive_cs, like the streaming paths do.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/865
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/quartz_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/quartz_transform.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/quartz_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/quartz_transform.c
@@ -271,12 +271,14 @@
     {
         IMemAllocator_Decommit(filter->source.pAllocator);
 
-        EnterCriticalSection(&filter->receive_cs);
+        /* Receive() and EndOfStream() take receive_cs while strmbase already
+         * holds stream_cs, so take them in the same order here. */
         EnterCriticalSection(&filter->filter.stream_cs);
+        EnterCriticalSection(&filter->receive_cs);
         winedmo_transform_destroy(filter->winedmo_transform);
         filter->winedmo_transform.handle = 0;
-        LeaveCriticalSection(&filter->filter.stream_cs);
         LeaveCriticalSection(&filter->receive_cs);
+        LeaveCriticalSection(&filter->filter.stream_cs);
     }
 
     return S_OK;
